dupefinder (2.5.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Image comparison runs as a numpy matrix product, about 6 times faster.
  * Files are read on all CPU cores.

 -- matthew <firefoxx.ms@gmail.com>  Wed, 28 Oct 2026 10:00:00 +0000

dupefinder (2.5.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Similar images match rotated and cropped copies (256-bit hashes, default
    threshold 16).
  * Similar videos sample a frame every two seconds, skip blank frames, and
    match cropped copies (default threshold 70).
  * Similar documents default to 70%, so edited copies are found.
  * Groups only join files that match every member, so unrelated files no
    longer end up together through a chain of matches.

 -- matthew <firefoxx.ms@gmail.com>  Mon, 26 Oct 2026 10:00:00 +0000

dupefinder (2.4.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * dupefinder-cli --apply refuses to trash more than --max-files copies
    (default 500).
  * --hardlink-plan lists copies that could become hard links on the same drive.
  * --mail-to emails the HTML report through an SMTP server.
  * README with install, usage, cleanup safety and file locations.

 -- matthew <firefoxx.ms@gmail.com>  Tue, 20 Oct 2026 19:00:00 +0000

dupefinder (2.3.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Keep rules: prefer clean names and prefer the best version (resolution
    or bitrate). RAW and JPEG pairs in one folder are protected by default.
  * Filters for maximum size, modification age, and .dupeignore files.
  * Parallel hashing, dry-run preview, select copies by rule, and an action
    history.
  * Cleanup and live-watch modes in dupefinder-cli, with webhook alerts.
  * Excel export, a command palette (Ctrl+K), and a Nemo right-click action.

 -- matthew <firefoxx.ms@gmail.com>  Tue, 20 Oct 2026 09:00:00 +0000

dupefinder (2.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Group results by the month a photo was taken.
  * Disk usage map drills into folders, with an Up button.
  * CLI output is flushed as it is printed, so watch mode output survives
    being piped or stopped.
  * Spanish translation covers the new labels.

 -- matthew <firefoxx.ms@gmail.com>  Mon, 19 Oct 2026 17:00:00 +0000

dupefinder (2.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Ignore groups you have reviewed, check bytes before grouping, and keep
    the copy inside a chosen folder.
  * Restore files from the trash, quarantine folder, and custom commands
    per file.
  * Scheduled scans through a systemd user timer, and a watch mode.
  * Similar audio mode, reclaimable space by file type, and a disk usage map.
  * Photo date and camera columns, thumbnails, saved scan profiles, and a
    high contrast theme.
  * Spanish translation for the main interface.

 -- matthew <firefoxx.ms@gmail.com>  Mon, 19 Oct 2026 16:00:00 +0000

dupefinder (2.0.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Dark and light themes, text size, remembered window size and recent
    folders.
  * Keyboard shortcuts, right-click menu, selection summary, and drag a
    folder onto the window.
  * Pause and resume scans, time left, skip patterns, subfolder depth limit.
  * Similar documents and similar videos modes; name-clash report.
  * Hard-link copies, move to a folder with undo, save and load results.
  * HTML report export, full-size image view, side-by-side compare, photo
    details.
  * Hex view for binary files; video previews cover about 30 formats.
  * New dupefinder-cli command for scripts.

